{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014XKjVybnAPD5nx7ER5FdcH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd111-ptx\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/ptx: Produce a Permuted Index\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS does not ship ptx. GNU ptx produces a permuted (keyword-in-context) index of\n6\t  text input. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gptx,\n7\t  installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n8\t\n9\tgoals:\n10\t  - G1: Produce a permuted (KWIC) index from text input.\n11\t  - G2: Support output width, gap size, and reference control.\n12\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gptx via differential testing.\n13\t\n14\trequirements:\n15\t  R1:\n16\t    title: KWIC index generation\n17\t    items:\n18\t      - R1.1:\n19\t          text: Must read input lines and produce a permuted index where each significant word appears as a keyword in context, with the surrounding text shown on either side.\n20\t\n21\t  R2:\n22\t    title: Index options\n23\t    items:\n24\t      - R2.1:\n25\t          text: \"-w N or --width=N must set the output line width (default 72). -g N or --gap-size=N must set the minimum gap between columns (default 3).\"\n26\t      - R2.2:\n27\t          text: \"-f or --ignore-case must fold lowercase to uppercase for sorting purposes.\"\n28\t      - R2.3:\n29\t          text: Must read from FILE or stdin when no file or \"-\" is given.\n30\t\n31\t  R3:\n32\t    title: Word regexp\n33\t    items:\n34\t      - R3.1:\n35\t          text: \"-W REGEXP or --word-regexp=REGEXP must use REGEXP to define what constitutes a word.\"\n36\t\n37\t  R4:\n38\t    title: Reference control\n39\t    items:\n40\t      - R4.1:\n41\t          text: \"-A or --auto-reference must produce automatically generated references based on file name and line number.\"\n42\t      - R4.2:\n43\t          text: \"-r or --references must treat the first field of each line as a reference and exclude it from the index.\"\n44\t\n45\t  R5:\n46\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n47\t    items:\n48\t      - R5.1:\n49\t          text: Must exit 0 on success. Must exit 1 on any error.\n50\t      - R5.2:\n51\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n52\t\n53\tnon_goals:\n54\t  - cmd/ptx does not implement TeX/roff output format in this release.\n55\t\n56\tacceptance_criteria:\n57\t  - id: AC1\n58\t    criterion: \"ptx on a text file produces a permuted index, matching gptx.\"\n59\t    traces:\n60\t      - R1.1\n61\t      - R2.3\n62\t  - id: AC2\n63\t    criterion: \"ptx -f folds case for sorting, matching gptx -f.\"\n64\t    traces:\n65\t      - R2.2\n66\t  - id: AC3\n67\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gptx passes.\"\n68\t    traces:\n69\t      - R1.1\n70\t  - id: AC4\n71\t    criterion: \"cmd/ptx compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n72\t    traces:\n73\t      - R1.1\n74\t      - R2.1\n75\t      - R2.2\n76\t      - R2.3\n77\t      - R3.1\n78\t      - R4.1\n79\t      - R4.2\n80\t      - R5.1\n81\t      - R5.2\n82\t\n83\tpackage_contract:\n84\t  imports:\n85\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f17556fc-f132-4e28-8c95-924585904c58","uuid":"1f488868-718a-48fb-b3b0-dac2c5fb161d","timestamp":"2026-05-30T16:23:59.467Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5672/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd111-ptx.yaml","content":"id: srd111-ptx\ntitle: \"cmd/ptx: Produce a Permuted Index\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS does not ship ptx. GNU ptx produces a permuted (keyword-in-context) index of\n  text input. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gptx,\n  installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Produce a permuted (KWIC) index from text input.\n  - G2: Support output width, gap size, and reference control.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gptx via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: KWIC index generation\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must read input lines and produce a permuted index where each significant word appears as a keyword in context, with the surrounding text shown on either side.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Index options\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-w N or --width=N must set the output line width (default 72). -g N or --gap-size=N must set the minimum gap between columns (default 3).\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-f or --ignore-case must fold lowercase to uppercase for sorting purposes.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must read from FILE or stdin when no file or \"-\" is given.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Word regexp\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-W REGEXP or --word-regexp=REGEXP must use REGEXP to define what constitutes a word.\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Reference control\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: \"-A or --auto-reference must produce automatically generated references based on file name and line number.\"\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"-r or --references must treat the first field of each line as a reference and exclude it from the index.\"\n\n  R5:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R5.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 on success. Must exit 1 on any error.\n      - R5.2:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/ptx does not implement TeX/roff output format in this release.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"ptx on a text file produces a permuted index, matching gptx.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.3\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"ptx -f folds case for sorting, matching gptx -f.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gptx passes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/ptx compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R5.1\n      - R5.2\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":86,"startLine":1,"totalLines":86}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HBvuLCadbQXwQ8VjtdwnwK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\t// cmd/ptx implements srd111-ptx: produce a permuted (KWIC) index of text input.\n5\tpackage main\n6\t\n7\timport (\n8\t\t\"bufio\"\n9\t\t\"errors\"\n10\t\t\"fmt\"\n11\t\t\"io\"\n12\t\t\"os\"\n13\t\t\"regexp\"\n14\t\t\"sort\"\n15\t\t\"strconv\"\n16\t\t\"strings\"\n17\t\t\"syscall\"\n18\t\t\"unicode\"\n19\t\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n20\t\n21\t\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n22\t)\n23\t\n24\tconst (\n25\t\tdefaultWidth   = 72\n26\t\tdefaultGapSize = 3\n27\t)\n28\t\n29\ttype options struct {\n30\t\twidth      int\n31\t\tgapSize    int\n32\t\tignoreCase bool\n33\t\twordRegexp *regexp.Regexp\n34\t\tfiles      []string\n35\t}\n36\t\n37\ttype entry struct {\n38\t\tbefore  string\n39\t\tkwAfter string\n40\t\tsortKey string\n41\t}\n42\t\n43\ttype wordSpan struct {\n44\t\tstart, end int\n45\t}\n46\t\n47\tfunc main() {\n48\t\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n49\t\n50\t\topts, err := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n51\t\tif err != nil {\n52\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"ptx: %s\\n\", err)\n53\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n54\t\t}\n55\t\n56\t\tlines, err := readAllLines(opts.files)\n57\t\tif err != nil {\n58\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"ptx: %s\\n\", formatErr(err))\n59\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n60\t\t}\n61\t\n62\t\tentries := buildIndex(lines, opts.ignoreCase, opts.wordRegexp)\n63\t\tsort.SliceStable(entries, func(i, j int) bool {\n64\t\t\treturn entries[i].sortKey < entries[j].sortKey\n65\t\t})\n66\t\n67\t\tif err := writeOutput(entries, opts.width, opts.gapSize); err != nil {\n68\t\t\tif errors.Is(err, syscall.EPIPE) {\n69\t\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n70\t\t\t}\n71\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"ptx: %s\\n\", formatErr(err))\n72\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n73\t\t}\n74\t}\n75\t\n76\tfunc parseArgs(args []string) (options, error) {\n77\t\topts := options{\n78\t\t\twidth:   defaultWidth,\n79\t\t\tgapSize: defaultGapSize,\n80\t\t}\n81\t\ti := 0\n82\t\tfor i < len(args) {\n83\t\t\ta := args[i]\n84\t\t\tif a == \"--\" {\n85\t\t\t\ti++\n86\t\t\t\tbreak\n87\t\t\t}\n88\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(a, \"--\") {\n89\t\t\t\tn, err := parseLongFlag(a, args[i+1:], &opts)\n90\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n91\t\t\t\t\treturn opts, err\n92\t\t\t\t}\n93\t\t\t\ti += 1 + n\n94\t\t\t\tcontinue\n95\t\t\t}\n96\t\t\tif a != \"-\" && strings.HasPrefix(a, \"-\") {\n97\t\t\t\tn, err := parseShortFlags(a[1:], args[i+1:], &opts)\n98\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n99\t\t\t\t\treturn opts, err\n100\t\t\t\t}\n101\t\t\t\ti += 1 + n\n102\t\t\t\tcontinue\n103\t\t\t}\n104\t\t\tbreak\n105\t\t}\n106\t\topts.files = args[i:]\n107\t\tif len(opts.files) == 0 {\n108\t\t\topts.files = []string{\"-\"}\n109\t\t}\n110\t\treturn opts, nil\n111\t}\n112\t\n113\tfunc parseLongFlag(flag string, rest []string, opts *options) (int, error) {\n114\t\tif flag == \"--ignore-case\" {\n115\t\t\topts.ignoreCase = true\n116\t\t\treturn 0, nil\n117\t\t}\n118\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(flag, \"--width=\") {\n119\t\t\treturn 0, parseIntVal(flag[len(\"--width=\"):], &opts.width, \"width\")\n120\t\t}\n121\t\tif flag == \"--width\" {\n122\t\t\tif len(rest) == 0 {\n123\t\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"option '%s' requires an argument\", flag)\n124\t\t\t}\n125\t\t\treturn 1, parseIntVal(rest[0], &opts.width, \"width\")\n126\t\t}\n127\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(flag, \"--gap-size=\") {\n128\t\t\treturn 0, parseIntVal(flag[len(\"--gap-size=\"):], &opts.gapSize, \"gap-size\")\n129\t\t}\n130\t\tif flag == \"--gap-size\" {\n131\t\t\tif len(rest) == 0 {\n132\t\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"option '%s' requires an argument\", flag)\n133\t\t\t}\n134\t\t\treturn 1, parseIntVal(rest[0], &opts.gapSize, \"gap-size\")\n135\t\t}\n136\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(flag, \"--word-regexp=\") {\n137\t\t\treturn 0, parseRegexpVal(flag[len(\"--word-regexp=\"):], &opts.wordRegexp)\n138\t\t}\n139\t\tif flag == \"--word-regexp\" {\n140\t\t\tif len(rest) == 0 {\n141\t\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"option '%s' requires an argument\", flag)\n142\t\t\t}\n143\t\t\treturn 1, parseRegexpVal(rest[0], &opts.wordRegexp)\n144\t\t}\n145\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"unrecognized option '%s'\", flag)\n146\t}\n147\t\n148\tfunc parseShortFlags(flags string, rest []string, opts *options) (int, error) {\n149\t\tfor i := 0; i < len(flags); i++ {\n150\t\t\tswitch flags[i] {\n151\t\t\tcase 'f':\n152\t\t\t\topts.ignoreCase = true\n153\t\t\tcase 'w':\n154\t\t\t\treturn extractAndSetInt(flags[i+1:], rest, &opts.width, 'w')\n155\t\t\tcase 'g':\n156\t\t\t\treturn extractAndSetInt(flags[i+1:], rest, &opts.gapSize, 'g')\n157\t\t\tcase 'W':\n158\t\t\t\treturn extractAndSetRegexp(flags[i+1:], rest, &opts.wordRegexp)\n159\t\t\tdefault:\n160\t\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid option -- '%c'\", flags[i])\n161\t\t\t}\n162\t\t}\n163\t\treturn 0, nil\n164\t}\n165\t\n166\tfunc extractAndSetInt(tail string, rest []string, dst *int, flag byte) (int, error) {\n167\t\tval, consumed, err := extractFlagValue(tail, rest, flag)\n168\t\tif err != nil {\n169\t\t\treturn 0, err\n170\t\t}\n171\t\tif err := parseIntVal(val, dst, string(flag)); err != nil {\n172\t\t\treturn 0, err\n173\t\t}\n174\t\treturn consumed, nil\n175\t}\n176\t\n177\tfunc extractFlagValue(tail string, rest []string, flag byte) (string, int, error) {\n178\t\tif tail != \"\" {\n179\t\t\treturn tail, 0, nil\n180\t\t}\n181\t\tif len(rest) > 0 {\n182\t\t\treturn rest[0], 1, nil\n183\t\t}\n184\t\treturn \"\", 0, fmt.Errorf(\"option requires an argument -- '%c'\", flag)\n185\t}\n186\t\n187\tfunc extractAndSetRegexp(tail string, rest []string, dst **regexp.Regexp) (int, error) {\n188\t\tval, consumed, err := extractFlagValue(tail, rest, 'W')\n189\t\tif err != nil {\n190\t\t\treturn 0, err\n191\t\t}\n192\t\tif err := parseRegexpVal(val, dst); err != nil {\n193\t\t\treturn 0, err\n194\t\t}\n195\t\treturn consumed, nil\n196\t}\n197\t\n198\tfunc parseRegexpVal(s string, dst **regexp.Regexp) error {\n199\t\tre, err := regexp.Compile(s)\n200\t\tif err != nil {\n201\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"invalid word regexp '%s': %s\", s, err)\n202\t\t}\n203\t\t*dst = re\n204\t\treturn nil\n205\t}\n206\t\n207\tfunc parseIntVal(s string, dst *int, name string) error {\n208\t\tv, err := strconv.Atoi(s)\n209\t\tif err != nil {\n210\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"invalid %s argument '%s'\", name, s)\n211\t\t}\n212\t\t*dst = v\n213\t\treturn nil\n214\t}\n215\t\n216\tfunc readAllLines(names []string) ([]string, error) {\n217\t\tvar all []string\n218\t\tfor _, name := range names {\n219\t\t\tlines, err := readFile(name)\n220\t\t\tif err != nil {\n221\t\t\t\treturn nil, err\n222\t\t\t}\n223\t\t\tall = append(all, lines...)\n224\t\t}\n225\t\treturn all, nil\n226\t}\n227\t\n228\tfunc readFile(name string) ([]string, error) {\n229\t\tvar r io.Reader\n230\t\tif name == \"-\" {\n231\t\t\tr = os.Stdin\n232\t\t} else {\n233\t\t\tf, err := os.Open(name)\n234\t\t\tif err != nil {\n235\t\t\t\treturn nil, err\n236\t\t\t}\n237\t\t\tdefer f.Close()\n238\t\t\tr = f\n239\t\t}\n240\t\tsc := bufio.NewScanner(r)\n241\t\tvar lines []string\n242\t\tfor sc.Scan() {\n243\t\t\tlines = append(lines, sc.Text())\n244\t\t}\n245\t\treturn lines, sc.Err()\n246\t}\n247\t\n248\tfunc buildIndex(lines []string, foldCase bool, wordRe *regexp.Regexp) []entry {\n249\t\tvar entries []entry\n250\t\tfor _, line := range lines {\n251\t\t\tfor _, w := range findWords(line, wordRe) {\n252\t\t\t\tsk := line[w.start:w.end]\n253\t\t\t\tif foldCase {\n254\t\t\t\t\tsk = strings.ToUpper(sk)\n255\t\t\t\t}\n256\t\t\t\tentries = append(entries, entry{\n257\t\t\t\t\tbefore:  line[:w.start],\n258\t\t\t\t\tkwAfter: line[w.start:],\n259\t\t\t\t\tsortKey: sk,\n260\t\t\t\t})\n261\t\t\t}\n262\t\t}\n263\t\treturn entries\n264\t}\n265\t\n266\tfunc findWords(line string, wordRe *regexp.Regexp) []wordSpan {\n267\t\tif wordRe != nil {\n268\t\t\treturn findWordsRegexp(line, wordRe)\n269\t\t}\n270\t\tvar spans []wordSpan\n271\t\ti := 0\n272\t\tfor i < len(line) {\n273\t\t\tr, size := utf8.DecodeRuneInString(line[i:])\n274\t\t\tif !isWordChar(r) {\n275\t\t\t\ti += size\n276\t\t\t\tcontinue\n277\t\t\t}\n278\t\t\tstart := i\n279\t\t\tfor i < len(line) {\n280\t\t\t\tr, size = utf8.DecodeRuneInString(line[i:])\n281\t\t\t\tif !isWordChar(r) {\n282\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n283\t\t\t\t}\n284\t\t\t\ti += size\n285\t\t\t}\n286\t\t\tspans = append(spans, wordSpan{start, i})\n287\t\t}\n288\t\treturn spans\n289\t}\n290\t\n291\tfunc findWordsRegexp(line string, re *regexp.Regexp) []wordSpan {\n292\t\tlocs := re.FindAllStringIndex(line, -1)\n293\t\tspans := make([]wordSpan, len(locs))\n294\t\tfor i, loc := range locs {\n295\t\t\tspans[i] = wordSpan{loc[0], loc[1]}\n296\t\t}\n297\t\treturn spans\n298\t}\n299\t\n300\tfunc isWordChar(r rune) bool {\n301\t\treturn unicode.IsLetter(r)\n302\t}\n303\t\n304\tfunc writeOutput(entries []entry, width, gapSize int) error {\n305\t\tw := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\n306\t\thalf := width / 2\n307\t\trightMax := width - half - gapSize\n308\t\tfor _, e := range entries {\n309\t\t\tline := formatEntry(e, half, gapSize, rightMax)\n310\t\t\tif _, err := w.WriteString(line); err != nil {\n311\t\t\t\treturn err\n312\t\t\t}\n313\t\t\tif err := w.WriteByte('\\n'); err != nil {\n314\t\t\t\treturn err\n315\t\t\t}\n316\t\t}\n317\t\treturn w.Flush()\n318\t}\n319\t\n320\tfunc formatEntry(e entry, half, gapSize, rightMax int) string {\n321\t\tleft := strings.TrimRight(e.before, \" \")\n322\t\tleftMax := max(half-gapSize, 0)\n323\t\tif len(left) > leftMax {\n324\t\t\tleft = left[len(left)-leftMax:]\n325\t\t}\n326\t\tright := e.kwAfter\n327\t\tif rightMax > 0 && len(right) > rightMax {\n328\t\t\tright = right[:rightMax]\n329\t\t}\n330\t\tvar buf strings.Builder\n331\t\twriteSpaces(&buf, half-len(left))\n332\t\tbuf.WriteString(left)\n333\t\twriteSpaces(&buf, gapSize)\n334\t\tbuf.WriteString(right)\n335\t\treturn buf.String()\n336\t}\n337\t\n338\tfunc writeSpaces(b *strings.Builder, n int) {\n339\t\tfor range n {\n340\t\t\tb.WriteByte(' ')\n341\t\t}\n342\t}\n343\t\n344\tfunc formatErr(err error) string {\n345\t\tif pe, ok := errors.AsType[*os.PathError](err); ok {\n346\t\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s: %s\", pe.Path, pe.Err)\n347\t\t}\n348\t\treturn err.Error()\n349\t}\n350\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f17556fc-f132-4e28-8c95-924585904c58","uuid":"648ce1a0-0c86-4aba-9cf7-6d24c5edc047","timestamp":"2026-05-30T16:23:59.469Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5672/cmd/ptx/main.go","content":"// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// cmd/ptx implements srd111-ptx: produce a permuted (KWIC) index of text input.\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"bufio\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"regexp\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strconv\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"syscall\"\n\t\"unicode\"\n\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n)\n\nconst (\n\tdefaultWidth   = 72\n\tdefaultGapSize = 3\n)\n\ntype options struct {\n\twidth      int\n\tgapSize    int\n\tignoreCase bool\n\twordRegexp *regexp.Regexp\n\tfiles      []string\n}\n\ntype entry struct {\n\tbefore  string\n\tkwAfter string\n\tsortKey string\n}\n\ntype wordSpan struct {\n\tstart, end int\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\n\topts, err := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"ptx: %s\\n\", err)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\n\tlines, err := readAllLines(opts.files)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"ptx: %s\\n\", formatErr(err))\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\n\tentries := buildIndex(lines, opts.ignoreCase, opts.wordRegexp)\n\tsort.SliceStable(entries, func(i, j int) bool {\n\t\treturn entries[i].sortKey < entries[j].sortKey\n\t})\n\n\tif err := writeOutput(entries, opts.width, opts.gapSize); err != nil {\n\t\tif errors.Is(err, syscall.EPIPE) {\n\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t\t}\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"ptx: %s\\n\", formatErr(err))\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc parseArgs(args []string) (options, error) {\n\topts := options{\n\t\twidth:   defaultWidth,\n\t\tgapSize: defaultGapSize,\n\t}\n\ti := 0\n\tfor i < len(args) {\n\t\ta := args[i]\n\t\tif a == \"--\" {\n\t\t\ti++\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(a, \"--\") {\n\t\t\tn, err := parseLongFlag(a, args[i+1:], &opts)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn opts, err\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\ti += 1 + n\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif a != \"-\" && strings.HasPrefix(a, \"-\") {\n\t\t\tn, err := parseShortFlags(a[1:], args[i+1:], &opts)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn opts, err\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\ti += 1 + n\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tbreak\n\t}\n\topts.files = args[i:]\n\tif len(opts.files) == 0 {\n\t\topts.files = []string{\"-\"}\n\t}\n\treturn opts, nil\n}\n\nfunc parseLongFlag(flag string, rest []string, opts *options) (int, error) {\n\tif flag == \"--ignore-case\" {\n\t\topts.ignoreCase = true\n\t\treturn 0, nil\n\t}\n\tif strings.HasPrefix(flag, \"--width=\") {\n\t\treturn 0, parseIntVal(flag[len(\"--width=\"):], &opts.width, \"width\")\n\t}\n\tif flag == \"--width\" {\n\t\tif len(rest) == 0 {\n\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"option '%s' requires an argument\", flag)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn 1, parseIntVal(rest[0], &opts.width, \"width\")\n\t}\n\tif strings.HasPrefix(flag, \"--gap-size=\") {\n\t\treturn 0, parseIntVal(flag[len(\"--gap-size=\"):], &opts.gapSize, \"gap-size\")\n\t}\n\tif flag == \"--gap-size\" {\n\t\tif len(rest) == 0 {\n\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"option '%s' requires an argument\", flag)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn 1, parseIntVal(rest[0], &opts.gapSize, \"gap-size\")\n\t}\n\tif strings.HasPrefix(flag, \"--word-regexp=\") {\n\t\treturn 0, parseRegexpVal(flag[len(\"--word-regexp=\"):], &opts.wordRegexp)\n\t}\n\tif flag == \"--word-regexp\" {\n\t\tif len(rest) == 0 {\n\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"option '%s' requires an argument\", flag)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn 1, parseRegexpVal(rest[0], &opts.wordRegexp)\n\t}\n\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"unrecognized option '%s'\", flag)\n}\n\nfunc parseShortFlags(flags string, rest []string, opts *options) (int, error) {\n\tfor i := 0; i < len(flags); i++ {\n\t\tswitch flags[i] {\n\t\tcase 'f':\n\t\t\topts.ignoreCase = true\n\t\tcase 'w':\n\t\t\treturn extractAndSetInt(flags[i+1:], rest, &opts.width, 'w')\n\t\tcase 'g':\n\t\t\treturn extractAndSetInt(flags[i+1:], rest, &opts.gapSize, 'g')\n\t\tcase 'W':\n\t\t\treturn extractAndSetRegexp(flags[i+1:], rest, &opts.wordRegexp)\n\t\tdefault:\n\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid option -- '%c'\", flags[i])\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn 0, nil\n}\n\nfunc extractAndSetInt(tail string, rest []string, dst *int, flag byte) (int, error) {\n\tval, consumed, err := extractFlagValue(tail, rest, flag)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err\n\t}\n\tif err := parseIntVal(val, dst, string(flag)); err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err\n\t}\n\treturn consumed, nil\n}\n\nfunc extractFlagValue(tail string, rest []string, flag byte) (string, int, error) {\n\tif tail != \"\" {\n\t\treturn tail, 0, nil\n\t}\n\tif len(rest) > 0 {\n\t\treturn rest[0], 1, nil\n\t}\n\treturn \"\", 0, fmt.Errorf(\"option requires an argument -- '%c'\", flag)\n}\n\nfunc extractAndSetRegexp(tail string, rest []string, dst **regexp.Regexp) (int, error) {\n\tval, consumed, err := extractFlagValue(tail, rest, 'W')\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err\n\t}\n\tif err := parseRegexpVal(val, dst); err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err\n\t}\n\treturn consumed, nil\n}\n\nfunc parseRegexpVal(s string, dst **regexp.Regexp) error {\n\tre, err := regexp.Compile(s)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"invalid word regexp '%s': %s\", s, err)\n\t}\n\t*dst = re\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc parseIntVal(s string, dst *int, name string) error {\n\tv, err := strconv.Atoi(s)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"invalid %s argument '%s'\", name, s)\n\t}\n\t*dst = v\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc readAllLines(names []string) ([]string, error) {\n\tvar all []string\n\tfor _, name := range names {\n\t\tlines, err := readFile(name)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tall = append(all, lines...)\n\t}\n\treturn all, nil\n}\n\nfunc readFile(name string) ([]string, error) {\n\tvar r io.Reader\n\tif name == \"-\" {\n\t\tr = os.Stdin\n\t} else {\n\t\tf, err := os.Open(name)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tdefer f.Close()\n\t\tr = f\n\t}\n\tsc := bufio.NewScanner(r)\n\tvar lines []string\n\tfor sc.Scan() {\n\t\tlines = append(lines, sc.Text())\n\t}\n\treturn lines, sc.Err()\n}\n\nfunc buildIndex(lines []string, foldCase bool, wordRe *regexp.Regexp) []entry {\n\tvar entries []entry\n\tfor _, line := range lines {\n\t\tfor _, w := range findWords(line, wordRe) {\n\t\t\tsk := line[w.start:w.end]\n\t\t\tif foldCase {\n\t\t\t\tsk = strings.ToUpper(sk)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tentries = append(entries, entry{\n\t\t\t\tbefore:  line[:w.start],\n\t\t\t\tkwAfter: line[w.start:],\n\t\t\t\tsortKey: sk,\n\t\t\t})\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn entries\n}\n\nfunc findWords(line string, wordRe *regexp.Regexp) []wordSpan {\n\tif wordRe != nil {\n\t\treturn findWordsRegexp(line, wordRe)\n\t}\n\tvar spans []wordSpan\n\ti := 0\n\tfor i < len(line) {\n\t\tr, size := utf8.DecodeRuneInString(line[i:])\n\t\tif !isWordChar(r) {\n\t\t\ti += size\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tstart := i\n\t\tfor i < len(line) {\n\t\t\tr, size = utf8.DecodeRuneInString(line[i:])\n\t\t\tif !isWordChar(r) {\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\ti += size\n\t\t}\n\t\tspans = append(spans, wordSpan{start, i})\n\t}\n\treturn spans\n}\n\nfunc findWordsRegexp(line string, re *regexp.Regexp) []wordSpan {\n\tlocs := re.FindAllStringIndex(line, -1)\n\tspans := make([]wordSpan, len(locs))\n\tfor i, loc := range locs {\n\t\tspans[i] = wordSpan{loc[0], loc[1]}\n\t}\n\treturn spans\n}\n\nfunc isWordChar(r rune) bool {\n\treturn unicode.IsLetter(r)\n}\n\nfunc writeOutput(entries []entry, width, gapSize int) error {\n\tw := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\n\thalf := width / 2\n\trightMax := width - half - gapSize\n\tfor _, e := range entries {\n\t\tline := formatEntry(e, half, gapSize, rightMax)\n\t\tif _, err := w.WriteString(line); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err := w.WriteByte('\\n'); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn w.Flush()\n}\n\nfunc formatEntry(e entry, half, gapSize, rightMax int) string {\n\tleft := strings.TrimRight(e.before, \" \")\n\tleftMax := max(half-gapSize, 0)\n\tif len(left) > leftMax {\n\t\tleft = left[len(left)-leftMax:]\n\t}\n\tright := e.kwAfter\n\tif rightMax > 0 && len(right) > rightMax {\n\t\tright = right[:rightMax]\n\t}\n\tvar buf strings.Builder\n\twriteSpaces(&buf, half-len(left))\n\tbuf.WriteString(left)\n\twriteSpaces(&buf, gapSize)\n\tbuf.WriteString(right)\n\treturn buf.String()\n}\n\nfunc writeSpaces(b *strings.Builder, n int) {\n\tfor range n {\n\t\tb.WriteByte(' ')\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc formatErr(err error) string {\n\tif pe, ok := errors.AsType[*os.PathError](err); ok {\n\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s: %s\", pe.Path, pe.Err)\n\t}\n\treturn err.Error()\n}\n","numLines":350,"startLine":1,"totalLines":350}}}
