{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler orchestrator pipeline) is requesting implementation of task #5672: extending the `cmd/ptx` (Permuted Index) utility with requirements R4.1 and R4.2 from srd111-ptx. Specifically:\n   - **R4.1**: `-A` or `--auto-reference` must produce automatically generated references based on file name and line number.\n   - **R4.2**: `-r` or `--references` must treat the first field of each line as a reference and exclude it from the index.\n   \n   The task is a \"stitch\" code generation task. Git is managed externally. Only `cmd/ptx/main.go` should be modified. Acceptance criteria: `go build` and `go vet` must pass.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Permuted (KWIC - Keyword In Context) index generation\n   - GNU ptx reference behavior for `-A` (auto-reference) and `-r` (references) flags\n   - Differential testing against `gptx` (Homebrew GNU reference binary)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Manual flag parsing (no cobra - the existing code uses hand-rolled arg parsing)\n   - The execution constitution mandates: no function > 40 lines, no file > 500 lines, DRY enforcement, copyright header, write-all-then-build strategy\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd111-ptx.yaml**\n     - Contains all requirements for ptx. R4.1 and R4.2 are the target requirements.\n     - R4.1: `-A or --auto-reference must produce automatically generated references based on file name and line number.`\n     - R4.2: `-r or --references must treat the first field of each line as a reference and exclude it from the index.`\n     - Non-goals: TeX/roff output format not implemented in this release.\n\n   - **cmd/ptx/main.go** (existing, 350 lines)\n     - Already implements R1.1 (KWIC index), R2.1 (width/gap), R2.2 (case folding), R2.3 (file/stdin), R3.1 (word regexp), R5.1/R5.2 (exit codes/SIGPIPE)\n     - Key structs:\n       ```go\n       type options struct {\n           width      int\n           gapSize    int\n           ignoreCase bool\n           wordRegexp *regexp.Regexp\n           files      []string\n       }\n       type entry struct {\n           before  string\n           kwAfter string\n           sortKey string\n       }\n       type wordSpan struct {\n           start, end int\n       }\n       ```\n     - Key functions: `parseArgs`, `parseLongFlag`, `parseShortFlags`, `readAllLines`, `readFile`, `buildIndex`, `findWords`, `writeOutput`, `formatEntry`\n     - `readAllLines` returns flat `[]string` - loses file/line metadata needed for R4.1\n     - `buildIndex` takes `[]string` lines with no file/line tracking\n     - `formatEntry` formats without reference column\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - work had not begun when summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that implementing R4.1 requires restructuring input handling to preserve file name and line number metadata (currently `readAllLines` returns flat `[]string`)\n   - Identified that R4.2 requires parsing first field from each line as reference and excluding it from indexing\n   - Both features require adding a reference column to the output formatting in `formatEntry`\n   - Need to add `autoRef` and `references` bool fields to `options` struct\n   - Need to add flag parsing for `-A`/`--auto-reference` and `-r`/`--references`\n   - Need to add a `ref` field to the `entry` struct to carry reference text through to output\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - One massive task message containing the full project context, SRD specifications, architecture, execution constitution, coding standards, and task description for implementing srd111-ptx R4.1 and R4.2.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement R4.1 (`-A`/`--auto-reference`): auto-generate references from filename and line number\n   - Implement R4.2 (`-r`/`--references`): extract first field as reference, exclude from index\n   - Modify `options` struct to add `autoRef` and `references` fields\n   - Add flag parsing for `-A`, `--auto-reference`, `-r`, `--references`\n   - Restructure input reading to track file name and line number per line\n   - Modify `entry` struct to include reference string\n   - Modify `buildIndex` to handle reference extraction\n   - Modify `formatEntry`/`writeOutput` to include reference column in output\n   - Run `go build -o bin/ptx ./cmd/ptx/` and `go vet ./cmd/ptx/` to verify\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file and the existing `cmd/ptx/main.go` implementation. I was about to begin planning and implementing the changes to add R4.1 and R4.2 support. No code changes have been made yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement the changes to `cmd/ptx/main.go` to add R4.1 and R4.2 support. This involves:\n   1. Adding `autoRef bool` and `references bool` to the `options` struct\n   2. Adding flag parsing for `-A`/`--auto-reference` and `-r`/`--references` in `parseLongFlag` and `parseShortFlags`\n   3. Creating a struct to track input lines with file/line metadata (for `-A`)\n   4. Modifying `buildIndex` to extract first-field references (for `-r`) and pass through auto-references\n   5. Adding a `ref` field to `entry` struct\n   6. Modifying `formatEntry` to append reference text to the right side of output\n   7. Running `go build` and `go vet` to verify compilation\n\n   The task description states: \"Implement srd111-ptx requirement R4.1 exactly as specified in the SRD\" and \"Implement srd111-ptx requirement R4.2 exactly as specified in the SRD\", with design decision \"Extend the existing implementation -- do not rewrite code that already satisfies completed requirements.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like e